// std/measure.dag -- Unit/Quantity carrier (algebra-axis dimensional shape).
//
// Per Q-Unit-1..5 RATIFIED at gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4385412256 (2026-05-06)
// and Q-Unit-1-Recanvas RATIFIED at gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4385539791
// (outer carrier renamed from `Unit` to `Measure` to avoid collision with
// kernel `Unit` terminal-object type at `dsl/std/types.dag`).
//
// Authority: `docs/briefs/r3-substrate-s9-unit-quantity-carrier-canvas.md`
// (RATIFICATION banner). Worker brief:
// `docs/briefs/r3-substrate-unit-quantity-carrier-worker.md`.
//
// Scope (Phase-1 carrier landing):
//   - `Measure<Q, S>` — phantom-parameter carrier for dimensional types.
//   - `Quantity` — what is being measured (Time, Length, Mass, ...).
//   - `Scale` — SI decimal scale exponent (Atto..Exa, with `One` = 10^0).
//
// NOT in scope (deferred per brief):
//   - Aspect axis (PointKind / Magnitude / Instant / Rate) -> R4 C6.
//   - Scale-agnostic `Duration<S>` parametric form -> needs >=2 consumers.
//   - 3-axis `AlgebraMachineRoundingProduct` -> R4 C5.
//
// COMPOSITION (S9 Phase-3 reframe per Q-Unit-4 RATIFIED outer-Refined /
// inner-Measure):
//
//   Duration     := Refined<Measure<Time, One>,   non_negative>
//   Milliseconds := Refined<Measure<Time, Milli>, non_negative>
//   Seconds      := Duration  (collapse per Q-Unit-3 RATIFIED)
//
// Predicates apply at the Measure-typed level: `non_negative` is
// "this duration is non-negative", not "this Int that happens to be
// milliseconds is non-negative". This satisfies
// `feedback_reason_not_label` -- the predicate name is the label,
// the reason is "this carries time-unit semantics".

module std.measure

// --- Quantity: what is being measured -------------------------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 SCAFFOLD
// Reference: `docs/modeling-discipline.md#4-coproduct-dissolution`
//   "Any new Rust enum with N >= 2 variants must have a checkpoint
//   comment naming its classification (🟢/🟡/🔴), with a ledger entry
//   if GREEN or a named trigger if YELLOW."
//
// Dissolution trigger (Q-Unit-5 RATIFIED): "all Quantity values consumed
// by >= 1 Grounding emission rule". Until each value gates a real
// emission rule (Grounding consumer demonstrates need), the carrier
// is hand-modeled / speculative. Adding a new value without a
// corresponding emission rule violates
// `feedback_construction_over_ratchets`; new values require the P1
// substrate-fact-introduction procedure with named consumer demand.
type Quantity =
    Time
  | Length
  | Mass
  | Memory
  | Information
  | DataRate
  | Frequency
  | Count
  | Currency

// --- Scale: SI decimal scale exponent -------------------------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 SCAFFOLD
// Same dissolution trigger as `Quantity`: "all Scale values consumed by
// >= 1 Grounding emission rule" (Q-Unit-5 RATIFIED).
//
// `One` is the unscaled identity (10^0) -- RATIFIED rename from `Unit`
// per Q-Unit-1 to avoid shadowing the outer carrier name and the
// kernel terminal-object `Unit` type.
type Scale =
    Atto       // 10^-18
  | Femto      // 10^-15
  | Pico       // 10^-12
  | Nano       // 10^-9
  | Micro      // 10^-6
  | Milli      // 10^-3
  | One        // 10^0   (identity scale; RATIFIED rename from `Unit` per Q-Unit-1)
  | Kilo       // 10^3
  | Mega       // 10^6
  | Giga       // 10^9
  | Tera       // 10^12
  | Peta       // 10^15
  | Exa        // 10^18

// --- Measure<Q, S>: phantom-parameter dimensional carrier -----------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟢 PRIMITIVE
// Phantom-parameter carrier: widening adds Quantity / Scale values, not
// new Measure variants. The carrier itself has a single inhabitant per
// (Q, S) pairing; the type parameters tag dimensional semantics for the
// type system without runtime payload distinction at this layer.
// Per-target representation (Rust `std::time::Duration`, Python
// `datetime.timedelta`, Go `time.Duration`, etc.) is Grounding's job
// per Q-Unit-4 RATIFIED.
type Measure<Q, S>
